---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Brave for Good privacy policy — how we collect, use, and protect your personal information."
>

  <section class="bg-brand-navy text-white py-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-serif font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-gray-300 text-sm">Last updated: February 9, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 prose prose-lg prose-gray max-w-none">

      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-rust mb-6">BRAVE For Good Privacy Policy and Terms of Use</p>

      <p class="font-semibold">PLEASE READ THIS PRIVACY POLICY AND TERMS OF USE CAREFULLY BEFORE USING THE SITE.</p>

      <p>By using the BRAVE For Good website, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy and Terms of Use, and agree to be bound by it. If you do not agree to any of the terms contained in this Privacy Policy and Terms of Use, please do not access the BRAVE For Good website.</p>

      <p>When you visit or log in to our website, cookies and similar technologies may be used by our online data partners or vendors to associate these activities with other personal information they or others have about you, including by association with your email or home address. We (or service providers on our behalf) may then send communications and marketing to these email or home addresses. You may opt out of receiving this advertising by visiting <a href="https://app.retention.com/optout" class="text-brand-rust hover:underline">https://app.retention.com/optout</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Information Collected</h2>
      <p>When you register for events, make a donation, sign up for our newsletter, or send a request to us at BRAVE For Good, we may collect information from you. The types of information we collect include:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li>Contact information (such as your name, birthday, email address, postal address, telephone number, and any other personal data) that you provide by completing forms on the Website and/or when you register for events or create an account on the Website</li>
        <li>Information from surveys that we may, from time to time, conduct on the Website or in Emails for research purposes, if you choose to respond to, or participate in, them</li>
        <li>Event participation history and how you use our website</li>
        <li>Donation information and transaction details</li>
        <li>Technical information about your browser and device</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We partner with Microsoft Clarity and Microsoft Advertising to capture how you use and interact with our website through behavioral metrics, heatmaps, and session replay to improve and promote our nonprofit programs and services. Website usage data is captured using first and third-party cookies and other tracking technologies to determine the popularity of programs and online activity. Additionally, we use this information for site optimization, fraud/security purposes, and outreach. For more information about how Microsoft collects and uses your data, visit the Microsoft Privacy Statement.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>BRAVE For Good may use your personal information to enhance your experience with our programs and events, provide you with relevant information regarding event participation, donation receipts, and updates about our mission and initiatives.</p>
      <p>BRAVE For Good does not rent or sell personal information to anyone, including third parties intending to use such information for direct marketing purposes. BRAVE For Good may share information with our third-party service providers that has been collected by but not limited to, account registration, cookies, web beacons, mobile device identifiers, embedded scripts, Google Analytics, A/B testing, payment processors, external social networks, event management platforms, and online survey platforms.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Retention of Your Personal Data</h2>
      <p>Our general approach is to retain your personal data only for as long as required to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected. We generally retain your personal data for no longer than three years from the end of our relationship or from the last contact from you (including event participation or donations), unless local law requires otherwise. However, in some circumstances, we may retain personal data for longer periods of time, for instance where we are required to do so in accordance with legal, tax, and accounting requirements. In specific circumstances, we may also retain your personal data for longer periods of time corresponding to the applicable statute of limitations so that we have an accurate record of your dealings with us in the event of any complaints or challenges.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the following rights with respect to your personal data:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Right to withdraw consent</strong> — where applicable, you have the right to withdraw your consent at any time. For example, if you wish to opt-out of receiving electronic marketing communications.</li>
        <li><strong>Right of access, rectification, and erasure</strong> — you have the right to request access to and obtain a copy of any of your personal data that we may hold, to request correction of any inaccurate data relating to you, and to request the deletion of your personal data under certain circumstances. You can see and update most of this data yourself online, or by contacting us at <a href="mailto:info@braveforgood.org" class="text-brand-rust hover:underline">info@braveforgood.org</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Right of data portability</strong> — under certain conditions, you have the right to receive all such personal data which you have provided to us in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format, and also to require us to transmit it to another controller where this is technically feasible.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to restriction of processing</strong> — you have the right to restrict our processing of your personal data in certain circumstances.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to object to processing justified on legitimate interest grounds</strong> — where we are relying upon legitimate interest to process personal data, you have the right to object to that processing.</li>
        <li>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority if you consider that the processing of your personal data infringes applicable law.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For further information or to exercise any of your rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@braveforgood.org" class="text-brand-rust hover:underline">info@braveforgood.org</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Protection of Information</h2>
      <p>Protecting your information is very important to us. The BRAVE For Good website uses secure socket layer (SSL) technology and other security measures to provide for the secure transmission of information from your device to our servers. We work with reputable payment processors to encrypt your payment information and other personal information.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Managing Your Personal Information</h2>
      <p>To access and edit your personal profile information, simply sign in to your account using your email address and password. You can review and change certain personal information related to your use of the BRAVE For Good website such as your name and contact information.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">California Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p>California Civil Code Section 1798.83 permits users of the Site who are California residents to request certain information regarding our disclosure of personal information to third parties for their direct marketing purposes. To make such a request, please contact us at <a href="mailto:info@braveforgood.org" class="text-brand-rust hover:underline">info@braveforgood.org</a> or write us at the address below.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Email Marketing</h2>
      <p>If you opt-in, we may send you direct email communications for program news, event announcements, and other information related to our mission. If you wish to stop receiving these emails, you can unsubscribe using the link provided in each email.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">What Do We Do With Your Information?</h2>
      <p>We may share your personal information as contemplated in our privacy policy, if you consent to us doing so, as well as in the following circumstances:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Third Parties that Help Provide Our Services.</strong> We may share your personal information with third parties that help us provide our nonprofit services (including, but not limited to, website platform providers, event management platforms, email service providers, donation processors, and other vendors who assist us in delivering our programs and communications).</li>
        <li><strong>Legal Requirements, Disclosures to Protect Us or Others.</strong> We may disclose any information we store associated with you to external parties if we, in good faith, believe doing so is required or appropriate to: comply with law enforcement or national security requests and legal process, such as a court order or subpoena; protect your, our, or others' rights, property, or safety; enforce our policies or contracts; collect amounts owed to us; or assist with an investigation or prosecution of suspected or actual illegal activity.</li>
        <li><strong>Email marketing:</strong> With your permission, we may send you emails about our programs, events and other updates.</li>
        <li><strong>Text marketing:</strong> With your permission, we may send text messages about our events, programs, and other updates. Updates may include event reminders.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Information from Children</h2>
      <p>BRAVE For Good's website is not targeted to or intended for use by children under the age of 13. BRAVE For Good will never knowingly request personally identifiable information online from anyone under the age of 13 without prior verifiable parental consent. Our events and programs are family-oriented and designed to be attended by children with their parents or guardians.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Transfer of Assets</h2>
      <p>In the case of organizational restructuring, merger, or acquisition, personally identifiable information and non-personal information we have about our supporters and participants may be transferred to and used by the successor entity, subject to this Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Trademarks</h2>
      <p>Unless otherwise noted, all materials, including images, photographs, videos, illustrations, and written material are copyrights, trademarks, names, logos, service marks, and trade names owned by BRAVE For Good.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">External Links</h2>
      <p>External links may be provided for your convenience, but they are beyond the control of BRAVE For Good. The inclusion of any link does not imply endorsement by BRAVE For Good of the site. Use of any such linked website is at the user's own risk, and BRAVE For Good is not responsible for the content or privacy policies on any non-BRAVE For Good sites to which the Site links.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Warranties</h2>
      <p>BRAVE For Good makes no warranties, representations, statements, or guarantees (whether express, implied in law, or residual) regarding the website.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>BRAVE For Good shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary injury, loss, claim, or damage that results from the use of, or incorrect use of, BRAVE For Good programs, the BRAVE For Good website or BRAVE For Good content.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Errors, Inaccuracies, and Omissions</h2>
      <p>Occasionally, there may be information on the BRAVE For Good website that contains typographical errors, inaccuracies, or omissions that may relate to program descriptions, event details, or availability. We reserve the right to correct any errors, inaccuracies, or omissions and to change or update information at any time without prior notice.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Use of Site</h2>
      <p>You may only use the BRAVE For Good website for your personal and non-commercial use in connection with learning about and supporting our nonprofit mission. Harassment, defaming, abusing, threatening, or using obscene or abusive language in any manner or form on the site is strictly forbidden.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>You agree not to copy or reproduce, or cause to be copied or reproduced, either directly or indirectly, BRAVE For Good content, program materials, branding, or images without express written permission.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Indemnification</h2>
      <p>You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless BRAVE For Good, its affiliates, directors, officers, volunteers, agents, and employees from and against any and all claims, damages, costs, and expenses, including attorneys' fees, arising from or related to your use of the BRAVE For Good website and/or violation of these Terms and Conditions or Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Termination</h2>
      <p>These Terms and Conditions are effective unless and until terminated by either you or BRAVE For Good. You may terminate this Agreement at any time, after which you agree that you shall not access the BRAVE For Good website. BRAVE For Good may terminate this Agreement at any time, may do so immediately, without notice, and may deny you access to the site.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Modifications to Privacy Policy and Terms of Use</h2>
      <p>BRAVE For Good may modify this Privacy Policy and Terms of Service occasionally at our sole discretion. If we make a material change to this Privacy Policy, we will post such changes on our Site. By continuing to use our Site after such notice, you are bound by this Privacy Policy as modified.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-brand-navy mt-10 mb-4">Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have questions, comments, requests, or concerns relating to this Privacy Policy, you may contact BRAVE For Good via <a href="mailto:info@braveforgood.org" class="text-brand-rust hover:underline">info@braveforgood.org</a> or mail:</p>
      <address class="not-italic mt-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        BRAVE For Good<br />
        Privacy Policy<br />
        100 Interstate 45 North, Suite 260<br />
        Conroe, TX 77301
      </address>

      <div class="mt-14 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-500">
        <p>Privacy Policy and Terms of Service last updated: February 9, 2026</p>
        <p class="mt-1">© 2025 Brave for Good, a not-for-profit, section 501(c)(3)</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
